    "sentence_translations": [
      "Do Chinese people celebrate Valentine's Day?",
      "",
      "February 14th is Valentine's Day, a holiday westerners like to celebrate.",
      "In China, Valentine's Day is not on February 14th, but the 7th day of the 7th month of the lunar calendar.",
      "This is also called the Chinese Valentine's Day.",
      "But nowadays many young Chinese people do not like celebrating the Chinese Valentine's day.",
      "Instead they prefer to celebrate Valentine's day on February 14th, together with westerners.",
      "",
      "On February 14th, the boyfriend usually hands a gift to the girlfriend.",
      "The gift can be roses, chocolate, etc.",
      "Roses represent love, and chocolate represents sweet sweet love.",
      "The Chinese like to give 9, 99, or 999 roses to their girlfriend, ..",
      ".. because 9 is pronounced the same as the character in “long”, symbolizing that their love will last for a long time.",
      "",
      "But because flowers are very expensive to buy on Valentine's day, a lot of young people do not buy flowers.",
      "Instead they choose to go to a nice restaurant and have a meal."
    ]
